why to use  react and when not to use -

when ui is a complex and dynamic state that change frequently like dashboard with live data, filter and interactive component.
as you know react work on virtual dom model 

working to react- when the state/props change , react re run  the  function component and produce the virtual dom - a lightweight js object tree ,not actual actual browser ,then check the change  from real dom and virtual dom , after that it commit only those to change to real dom. that is why react is faster because it didn't touch the real dom until unless the change are made.

note -React uses a Diffing Algorithm to compare the old Virtual DOM and new Virtual DOM. It identifies only the changed elements and updates only those parts in the real DOM, which improves performance.


when not to use react - not for static page in which nothing change like landing page /blog page 


